hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28169","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman meaning Ibn Abi al-Mawali narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi, on the authority of his grandmother Salma, servant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I never heard anyone complain to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of pain in his head except he said: Cup, nor pain in his legs except he said: Dye them with henna."
"28170","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali narrated to us, Faid, freedman of Banu Rafi, narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn Ubaydillah ibn Abi Rafi, on the authority of his aunt Salma, she said: No one complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of pain in his head except he said: Cup, and no one complained to him of pain in his legs except he said: Dye your legs."
